MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Beatles 1 and Abbey Road feel like natural next choices because I previously chose Sgt. Pepper's; another Beatles recording gives me a clear connection to music I already seek out.",
    "Eagles: The Very Best Of matches my repeated interest in melodic classic rock and greatest-hits collections, while Partners appeals to the vocal duet interest reflected in Cheek to Cheek."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Fallen, American Idiot, and St. Anger lean toward heavier or more aggressive sounds than the melodic classic pop, rock, and folk recordings I want now; sharing a broad rock connection is not enough.",
    "Adele's albums could appeal to my interest in pop vocals, but that connection is less compelling right now than the Beatles albums and familiar classic-rock collections."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in rock seems to have been stretched to include punk and aggressive metal, overlooking how much the sound and mood matter to my choices.",
    "My interest in Born This Way and Cheek to Cheek seems to have been treated as a broad appetite for contemporary pop, although those choices do not make every prominent vocal album an immediate match."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I repeatedly choose best-of collections and older melodic recordings, so the combination of familiar songs and a classic sound matters more than either connection alone.",
    "There is a difference between something I could enjoy and something I would choose now: Led Zeppelin IV fits my classic-rock interest, but the Beatles and Eagles selections are stronger immediate choices."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my Beatles, classic-rock, and vocal interests, but stretched those connections beyond my current preference for melodic older music and familiar collections."
}
